<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>HaulTimes</title><link>https://haultimes.com/</link><description>Freight and trucking news for the US and Canada</description><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:11:27 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Broker RXO says TL spot rates not entering deflationary phase</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/broker-rxo-says-tl-spot-rates-not-entering-deflationary-phase-a17334730a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/broker-rxo-says-tl-spot-rates-not-entering-deflationary-phase-a17334730a/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:13:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Rates &amp; Market</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>CBSA officers seize 81 kg of suspected cocaine from a commercial truck arriving from the US, at Pacific Highway</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/cbsa-officers-seize-81-kg-of-suspected-cocaine-from-a-commercial-truck-d57d869691/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/cbsa-officers-seize-81-kg-of-suspected-cocaine-from-a-commercial-truck-d57d869691/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>Canada Border Services Agency</description></item><item><title>Q3 2026 Cargo Theft Falls as Losses Rise</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/q3-2026-cargo-theft-falls-as-losses-rise-036656251d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/q3-2026-cargo-theft-falls-as-losses-rise-036656251d/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:55:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Verisk CargoNet reported 547 supply chain crime incidents involving cargo across the U.S. and Canada in the third quarter of 2026, down 33% from a year earlier and 19% from the second quarter. Estimated losses still rose 12% to $230.1 million. Fictitious pickups, in which criminals use deception to obtain a shipment, fell only 6% to 138, so their share of reported activity rose to about 25%.

Through September, reported incidents were down 25% year to date, while estimated losses rose 39% to $718.9 million. The average value of stolen goods with a documented value rose 72% to $448,456. CargoNet logged 19 thefts of $1 million or more, compared with nine a year earlier. California accounted for about a third of incidents, and four states made up 57% of the quarterly total. CargoNet also documented fraud schemes in 2026 that used compromised email accounts, internet phone systems and transportation applications, and said theft has historically risen in Q4.</description></item><item><title>Cass Freight Index: Freight cycle finds a higher gear</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/cass-freight-index-freight-cycle-finds-a-higher-gear-06303619b7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/cass-freight-index-freight-cycle-finds-a-higher-gear-06303619b7/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:49:43 +0000</pubDate><category>Rates &amp; Market</category><description>TheTrucker.com</description></item><item><title>The Right Tool for the Job: The Reality of AI in Freight</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/the-right-tool-for-the-job-the-reality-of-ai-in-freight-e333eb61f7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/the-right-tool-for-the-job-the-reality-of-ai-in-freight-e333eb61f7/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:48:41 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Petro-Canada PC-12 Engine Oils: What Fleets Need to Know for 2027</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/petro-canada-pc-12-engine-oils-what-fleets-need-to-know-for-2027-196e2beda6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/petro-canada-pc-12-engine-oils-what-fleets-need-to-know-for-2027-196e2beda6/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:40:13 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Saia asks FMCSA to allow CLP holder