Midwest had the largest, from $6.201 to $5.967. The article links the drop to slipping oil prices. On an early Tuesday, the Associated Press reported that Brent crude edged 49 cents lower to $92.93 a barrel and U.S. benchmark crude slid 51 cents to $86.23 per barrel.</description></item><item><title>New specific bonus for fuel tanker truck drivers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/new-specific-bonus-for-fuel-tanker-truck-drivers-379f9abb9a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/new-specific-bonus-for-fuel-tanker-truck-drivers-379f9abb9a/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:22:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Nessma TV</description></item><item><title>Truck Parking Club hands CPC 7 drop yards in two months</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-parking-club-hands-cpc-7-drop-yards-in-two-months-ac60a533be/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-parking-club-hands-cpc-7-drop-yards-in-two-months-ac60a533be/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:18:46 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Six commercial vehicles placed out of service in Ontario during enforcement blitz</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/six-commercial-vehicles-placed-out-of-service-in-ontario-during-enforc-9f6c87c542/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/six-commercial-vehicles-placed-out-of-service-in-ontario-during-enforc-9f6c87c542/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:14:57 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Shippers Are Finally Ready to Fix the Supply Chain Behind the Freight Bill</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/shippers-are-finally-ready-to-fix-the-supply-chain-behind-the-freight-f5ed5bdb3f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/shippers-are-finally-ready-to-fix-the-supply-chain-behind-the-freight-f5ed5bdb3f/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:05:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Manitoba trucking industry celebrates heroism and service</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/manitoba-trucking-industry-celebrates-heroism-and-service-cc704ee782/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/manitoba-trucking-industry-celebrates-heroism-and-service-cc704ee782/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:04:26 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>FleetWatcher adds driver certification tracking</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fleetwatcher-adds-driver-certification-tracking-4f383b61e4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fleetwatcher-adds-driver-certification-tracking-4f383b61e4/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:59:18 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Five Manitoba fleets join Trucking HR Canada’s Women’s Leadership Accord</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/five-manitoba-fleets-join-trucking-hr-canada-s-women-s-leadership-acco-1571d7c228/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/five-manitoba-fleets-join-trucking-hr-canada-s-women-s-leadership-acco-1571d7c228/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:45:36 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Man, 24, dies in head-on crash between semi-trailer and truck in Manitoba&#x27;s Interlake</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/man-24-dies-in-head-on-crash-between-semi-trailer-and-truck-in-manitob-3a17264ddd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/man-24-dies-in-head-on-crash-between-semi-trailer-and-truck-in-manitob-3a17264ddd/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:41:37 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>CBC</description></item><item><title>GTCC and Old Dominion Freight Line support future truckers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/gtcc-and-old-dominion-freight-line-support-future-truckers-27332026fc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/gtcc-and-old-dominion-freight-line-support-future-truckers-27332026fc/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:19:18 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Guilford Technical Community College in Greensboro runs a truck driver training program that staff say has grown every year since it started six years ago. The certificate takes eight weeks of full-time study or 14 weeks of nights and weekends, and costs about $1,800 including books. Jan Knox, VP of the college advancement foundation, said graduates can often find work right away at a salary of $60,000 or more.

Old Dominion Freight Line, a trucking company headquartered in the Triad, is funding four $1,000 scholarships a year at the college, two of them for women. Chris Brooks, Senior VP of HR at the company, said the awards help people who might not otherwise afford a CDL or a diesel mechanic certification. The company said it has over 200 women drivers.</description></item><item><title>US cargo theft falls 8% in Q3 as truck stop incidents nearly triple</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/us-cargo-theft-falls-8-in-q3-as-truck-stop-incidents-nearly-triple-bdd1f4a40c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/us-cargo-theft-falls-8-in-q3-as-truck-stop-incidents-nearly-triple-bdd1f4a40c/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:24 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>The &quot;Mighty Mitch&quot; Method: Logistics Growth, Tech, &amp; People — What The Truck?!?</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/the-mighty-mitch-method-logistics-growth-tech-people-what-the-truck-9d4c887eb0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/the-mighty-mitch-method-logistics-growth-tech-people-what-the-truck-9d4c887eb0/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:19:09 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Should Truck Drivers Have an Age Limit? The I-84 Rollover Debate — What The Truck?!?</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/should-truck-drivers-have-an-age-limit-the-i-84-rollover-debate-what-t-9b7c99251f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/should-truck-drivers-have-an-age-limit-the-i-84-rollover-debate-what-t-9b7c99251f/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:51:09 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Shift Supervisor - Logistics in Minneapolis, MN for Penske Truck Leasing</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/shift-supervisor-logistics-in-minneapolis-mn-for-penske-truck-leasing-55ca7af8e1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/shift-supervisor-logistics-in-minneapolis-mn-for-penske-truck-leasing-55ca7af8e1/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:10:50 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Higher diesel prices strain farm transportation budgets</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/higher-diesel-prices-strain-farm-transportation-budgets-e7952ede0c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/higher-diesel-prices-strain-farm-transportation-budgets-e7952ede0c/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:02:23 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>Higher diesel prices are adding costs for Iowa farmers and trucking operators, according to Matt Wells, vice president of the Mid-West Truckers Association. Wells cited refinery shutdowns, declining fuel reserves and the war between Russia and Ukraine as factors tightening supply. He said two California refineries were shut down and a refinery in Joliet, Illinois, was offline for seven to ten days, while Ukrainian attacks damaged Russian refining facilities.

Wells said transportation rates and operating budgets will need to reflect the higher costs, potentially for the next year to year and a half, and he does not expect diesel prices to fall significantly soon. He also cautioned that fuel prices do not always return to earlier levels after a large increase. On red-dyed diesel, Wells said the modern dyed product is essentially the same fuel as clear highway diesel, and that its use on public roads remains subject to federal and state tax requirements and any specifically authorized exemptions.</description></item><item><title>Detroit Diesel Promises 2027 Engines With No Penalties, 3% TCO Savings</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/detroit-diesel-promises-2027-engines-with-no-penalties-3-tco-savings-27e3bb0783/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/detroit-diesel-promises-2027-engines-with-no-penalties-3-tco-savings-27e3bb0783/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:44:02 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Cybersecurity Training for Fleets, AI Logistics Tools &amp; more</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/cybersecurity-training-for-fleets-ai-logistics-tools-more-aca4446e8b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/cybersecurity-training-for-fleets-ai-logistics-tools-more-aca4446e8b/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:48:56 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>How ATA Wants to Fix ELD Certification</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/how-ata-wants-to-fix-eld-certification-a812fcb144/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/how-ata-wants-to-fix-eld-certification-a812fcb144/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:51:16 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Heavy Duty Trucking</description></item><item><title>New York defeats FMCSA in major legal battle over non-domicil